===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|pl|Ukraina}} or {{bor|en|ru|Украи́на}}, from {{der|en|orv|оукраина}}, which is most commonly taken to have meant "borderland, {{l|en|march|marches|id=borderland}}" in this context, though for about a century now Ukrainian scholars have articulated an alternative theory that it meant "region, country, the land around (a given center)" in this context instead.<!--S. Shelukhin, "Україна — назва нашої землі з найдавніших часів", Prague, 1936. M. Andrusiak, "The name 'Ukraine': 'country' or 'outskirts'", Prague, 1941; History of the Cossacks, vol. 1-3, Munich; F. Shevchenko: "термін 'Україна', 'Вкраїна' має передусім значення 'край', 'країна', а не 'окраїна'" ("the term 'Ukraine', 'Ukraine' primarily means 'land', 'country', and not 'outskirts'"): volume 1, p. 189 in History of the Ukrainian SSR [in 8 volumes, 10 books; 1979].--> See {{w|Name of Ukraine}} for more.

