====Usage notes====
* Since the country's independence in 1991, style guides recommend {{m|en|Ukraine}} (as in “a musician from Ukraine”), without an article. Previously, the most common usage was ''the Ukraine'' (as in “a musician from the Ukraine”).<ref>{{cite-web
|title       = Ukraine or the Ukraine: Why do some country names have 'the'?
|date        = June 7, 2012
|work        = BBC News Magazine
|author      = Tom Geoghegan
|url         = http://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-18233844
|archiveurl  = https://web.archive.org/web/20161028152503/http://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-18233844
|archivedate = 28 October 2016
|accessdate  = July 07, 2017
}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web |en |url=https://time.com/12597/the-ukraine-or-ukraine/ |title=''Ukraine'', Not ''the Ukraine'': The Significance of Three Little Letters |work={{w|Time (magazine)|Time}} |date=2014-03-05 |accessdate=2022-12-06 |last=Steinmetz |first=Katy}}</ref>

